  "clues": {
    "kinetics": "A high-fat meal has no significant effect on exposure, lowering AUC by about 18% and Cmax by about 22%. Only about 4.7% is unbound in plasma, and it is cleared mainly by CYP3A4 metabolism.",
    "substance": "A white to off-white powder with a molecular weight of 603.5. It is practically insoluble in water.",
    "product": "An NDA product supplied as tablets of 10, 30 and 60 mg.",
    "safety": "No boxed warning. It is contraindicated in patients with a history of hypersensitivity to the drug or its components; nausea, constipation and fatigue or somnolence are the most common reactions.",
    "indication": "Preventive treatment of migraine in adults.",
    "mechanism": "It is an antagonist of the calcitonin gene-related peptide (CGRP) receptor, blocking the peptide's action."
  },
  "tell": "Itraconazole, a strong CYP3A4 inhibitor, raises this CGRP receptor antagonist's exposure 5.5-fold in AUC.",
